BT /F1 16.00 Tf 0.1216 0.2275 0.3725 rg 56.693 762.520 Td (Sewing guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.00 Tf 0.4000 0.4000 0.4000 rg 56.693 737.008 Td (custom measurements  .  4 pieces  .  2.15 m fabric at 140 cm wide) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.00 Tf 0.4000 0.4000 0.4000 rg 56.693 717.165 Td (text-first guide, no illustrations in this edition. Every step is the engine's own instruction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0.1216 0.2275 0.3725 rg 56.693 683.150 Td (Cut list) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 660.472 Td (Top Front - cut 1 on fold) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 644.598 Td (Top Back - cut 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 628.724 Td (Spaghetti Strap \(ince aski\) - cut 2 rectangle\(s\) 46 x 171 mm \(finished 8 mm wide, a plain self-lined tube at the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 612.850 Td (finished 141 mm strap span\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.50 Tf 0.1216 0.2275 0.3725 rg 56.693 596.976 Td (Strips / notions \(chalked on fabric, not printed\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 578.268 Td (Bias binding \(neckline + armholes\) - cut 1 strip\(s\) 1279 x 25 mm ON THE BIAS \(45° to the grain\), join end to end) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 562.394 Td (\(total 1279 mm = edge 1259 mm + overlap\), press in half, wrap the edge and trim the excess) Tj ET
BT /F1 13.00 Tf 0.1216 0.2275 0.3725 rg 56.693 523.843 Td (Construction order) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 501.165 Td (1. Print and check the 3 cm calibration square before cutting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 478.488 Td (2. This block uses standard assumptions for shoulder slope and underbust - sew a quick muslin first and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 462.614 Td (adjust before cutting your real fabric.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 439.937 Td (3. Cut every piece as labelled \('on fold' on the fabric fold, 'cut 2' twice\). Check the neck opening against your) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 424.063 Td (head circumference - a top has no zipper, it must slip over your head.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 401.386 Td (4. Staystitch the neckline just inside the seam line so it doesn't stretch while you work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 378.709 Td (5. Sew the shoulder seams and press them open.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 356.031 Td (6. Prepare the neckline bias strip: join the ends as needed and press it in half lengthwise along the marked) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 340.157 Td (fold line.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 317.480 Td (7. Bind the neckline with the bias strip, right sides together and raw edges even, easing the strip gently around) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 301.606 Td (the curves. Trim to 6 mm, turn the folded edge to the inside and topstitch or slipstitch it down.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 278.929 Td (8. Sew the side seams.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 256.252 Td (9. Finish each armhole with its bias strip: press it in half, bind the armhole right sides together, ease around) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 240.378 Td (the curve, then turn and topstitch it to the inside.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 217.701 Td (10. Hem with a 2 cm double fold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 56.693 195.024 Td (11. Spaghetti straps: cut the two strap rectangles as labelled. Fold each in half lengthwise right sides together,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 179.150 Td (stitch the long edge, turn right side out and press \(a plain self-lined tube, no gathering\). Stitch each end to its) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 163.276 Td (shoulder placement notch - one at the front, the other at the back - catching it in the top-edge seam. Cut on) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.50 Tf 0.0667 0.0667 0.0667 rg 73.701 147.402 Td (the straight grain.) Tj ET

